{"author":{"id":"8022379585b4ab99ca8775db3eb67d33fcb256817114c28e51ccc1e9f55cdec4"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1791471025,"nonce":"Pv8iZnrjFLtc7HdwO92r5M9uqGw=","title":"Builtin calls on a generic method result bypass runtime lowering","message":"Reproduced while checking abstract constructor forwarding. This also fails with an ordinary abstract constructor, so it is independent of @:forward.new.\n\nclass Main {\n  static function main() {\n    var wrapped = new Wrap\u003cArray\u003cInt\u003e\u003e([]);\n    wrapped.value().push(3);\n    Sys.println(wrapped.value().length);\n    var values = wrapped.value();\n    values.push(4);\n    Sys.println(values.length);\n    var regex = new Wrap\u003cEReg\u003e(new EReg(\"abc\", \"\"));\n    Sys.println(regex.value().match(\"abc\"));\n    var pattern = regex.value();\n    Sys.println(pattern.match(\"abc\"));\n  }\n}\nabstract Wrap\u003cT\u003e(T) {\n  public inline function new(value:T) this = value;\n  public function value():T return this;\n}\n\nNative Haxe prints 1, 2, true, true. Pinned Cranelift prints 0, 1, false, true. Assigning the generic return to a local allows the existing builtin lowering to work.\n\nStandalone probes: /tmp/ArrayReturnProbe.hx and /tmp/RegExpReturnProbe.hx, logs /tmp/rayzor-array-return-probe{,-native}.log and /tmp/rayzor-regexp-return-probe.log. In the constructor forwarding fixture, both Cranelift and LLVM exhibit the direct-call failure. MIR /tmp/rayzor-forward-new-mir-v2b.log emits no push at all and resolves match to EReg.match's constant-false standard-library body instead of the native runtime mapping. Forwarded construction itself creates the array and EReg correctly. Check receiver method lookup/runtime mapping for MethodCall receivers after generic result substitution.\n\nObserved on release build of HEAD b209d38174d1e1490d65f794668efe570e9c9efb plus pending constructor-forwarding changes. No corpus or harness changes.","files":null}]}